##
#
# Transonic flow around the ONERA OAT15a supercritical airfoil in 3D,
# Section 6.4 (Figure 3) of [3]; experiment of Jacquin et al. [1, 2].
#
# Free stream of air at Mach 0.73 with an angle of attack of 3.5 deg:
#
#   rho = 1.225 kg/m^3,  |v| = 248.42 m/s,  p = 1.013 10^5 N/m^2,
#   gamma = 1.401,  mu = 1.789 10^-5 Ns/m^2,  lambda = 0,
#   c_v^{-1} kappa = 3.616 10^-5 Ns/m^2.
#
# The chord length is 0.23 m (Reynolds number about 3 10^6) and the airfoil
# is extruded in z-direction over a width of 0.046 m (span to chord ratio
# 0.2). The mesh is graded towards the airfoil with x -> x^2. No-slip
# conditions are enforced on the airfoil and non-reflecting ("dynamic")
# conditions on the outer boundary. All boundaries are thermally insulated.
#
# The airfoil geometry makes the two z-planes periodic. [3] states slip
# conditions there, but the code of the time also used periodic faces.
#
# Physical and airfoil parameters are taken from the parameter file of the
# time (git 6241230f, May 2021). Mesh refinement 5 with 16 coarse
# subdivisions in z-direction gives about 535k gridpoints per z-slice and
# 512 slices, i.e. around 274M gridpoints as in [3]. The time stepping
# scheme follows today's defaults. This is a reconstruction, differences to
# the published results are expected.
#
# The pressure coefficient C_p of Figure 3 of [3] is a time average over
# 900 samples taken every δt = 10^-4 s, averaged in z-direction: the
# quantities task records the time and space averaged primitive state on
# the airfoil surface. The final time is t = 0.22 s and we output cut
# planes every δt = 0.005 s.
#
# The strong scaling tests of Section 6.5 (Figure 4) of [3] use this
# configuration on meshes with 4.36M to 17.4B gridpoints and measure the
# run time of 1000 time steps; use "max cycles = 1000", drop the output
# tasks, and change mesh refinement.
#
# [1] L. Jacquin, P. Molton, S. Deck, B. Maury, D. Soulevant. Experimental
#     study of shock oscillation over a transonic supercritical profile.
#     AIAA J. 47:1985-1994, 2009.
#
# [2] S. Deck, N. Renard. Towards an enhanced protection of attached
#     boundary layers in hybrid RANS/LES methods. J. Comput. Phys.
#     400:108970, 2020.
#
# [3] J.-L. Guermond, M. Kronbichler, M. Maier, B. Popov, I. Tomas. On the
#     implementation of a robust and efficient finite element-based
#     parallel solver for the compressible Navier-Stokes equations. Comput.
#     Methods Appl. Mech. Engrg., 389:114250, 2022. arXiv:2106.02159
#
##

subsection A - Scheduler
  set basename          = oat15a-3d

  set tasks             = vtu levelsets, quantities

  set final time        = 0.2200
  set timer granularity = 0.0001
end


subsection B - Equation
  set dimension = 3
  set equation  = navier stokes

  # Air at sea level
  set gamma     = 1.401
  set mu        = 1.789e-5
  set lambda    = 0
  # Scaled thermal conductivity c_v^{-1} kappa
  set kappa     = 3.616e-5
end


subsection C - Discretization
  set geometry        = airfoil
  set mesh refinement = 5

  subsection airfoil
    set airfoil type                        = ONERA OAT15a
    set airfoil center                      = -0.0613, 0.
    set airfoil length                      =  0.2300
    set psi center                          =  0.03, 0.
    set psi ratio                           =  3.00
    set height                              =  1.0
    set width                               =  0.046
    set grading exponent                    =  2.0000
    set grading epsilon                     =  0.0005
    set grading epsilon trailing            =  0.0100
    set anisotropic pre refinement airfoil  =  1
    set anisotropic pre refinement trailing =  3
    set subdivisions z                      =  16
  end
end


subsection E - InitialValues
  set configuration = uniform
  # 3.5deg angle of attack:
  set direction     = 0.99813, 0.061049, 0.
  set position      = 0., 0., 0.

  subsection uniform
    # Air at sea level and flow at Mach 0.73
    # rho [kg/m^3], v [m/s], p [N/m^2]
    set primitive state = 1.225, 248.42, 1.013e5
  end
end


subsection G - ParabolicModule
  set tolerance             = 1e-14
  set tolerance linfty norm = false
end


subsection I - VTUOutput
  subsection levelsets
    set manifolds          = x-0.075, x-0.15, y, y-0.01, y+0.01, z-0.023
    set trigger multiplier = 50
    set use mpi io         = true
    set schlieren beta     = 10
  end
end


subsection J - Quantities
  set boundary manifolds = \
    airfoil : floor(x*x/0.0266 + 36*y*y/0.0266) : time_averaged space_averaged
end
